  "limitations": [
    "Application timer covers fresh template training for compact representations, complete captured-TSV conversion and two routing batches, including validation and exports. CSR requires no template training.",
    "Excludes Vivado acquisition, board transfer and physical readback; these remain separate requirements. Training is rebuilt from the original3761 captured sources and must reproduce the frozen440-template bank exactly before reading the evaluation graph.",
    "Preflight integrity checks and post-route semantic audit are outside application timer but inside process wall.",
    "Parent conversion peak and native child peak are distinct process measurements; do not sum them as simultaneous memory.",
    "Parent drops graph/adapter objects before native launch. Shared host, page cache and buffered disk writes remain uncontrolled.",
    "Seven fresh processes per condition, randomized within each repeat block.",
    "Each application wall measures regeneration and TWO batches, not single-batch latency.",
    "All blocks run sequentially on one CPU; unrelated host workloads remain uncontrolled."
  ],
